{"parentUuid":"d3621be7-ff13-425d-9fea-d90835e0f4f8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a573a93d8823d4dbd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SMmaU7PPcWPH7ZRZcQVAGh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JJewdW6nh5xcemFZrw3mxS","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Dyson Sphere Program calculator blueprint optimizer solver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7970,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":331,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7970},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7970,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot4kQuUu85GmbPopNdN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3409710-a74a-4143-b41a-9b08deecdac6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:10.824Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d3621be7-ff13-425d-9fea-d90835e0f4f8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a573a93d8823d4dbd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GxSsA8JGRf8iJB6mk9nkKk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Satisfactory Tools calculator algorithm linear programming solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[SCIM] Satisfactory - Calculator | Gaming Tool/Wiki/Database to empower the players.\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory-calculator.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Production planner / [SCIM] Satisfactory - Calculator | Gaming Tool/Wiki/Database to empower the players.\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory-calculator.com/en/planners/production\"},{\"title\":\"Satisfactory Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory.greeny.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"Online tools - Satisfactory Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory.fandom.com/wiki/Online_tools\"},{\"title\":\"[1.0] Satisfactory Tools\",\"url\":\"https://www.satisfactorytools.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Online tools - Official Satisfactory Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory.wiki.gg/wiki/Online_tools\"},{\"title\":\"Satisfactory - Calculator / AnthorNet - FullStack Web Developer\",\"url\":\"https://anthor.net/en/satisfactory\"},{\"title\":\"Tools / [SCIM] Satisfactory - Calculator | Gaming Tool/Wiki/Database to empower the players.\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory-calculator.com/en/tools\"},{\"title\":\"Linear Programming Solver - Simplex Method with Graphical Feasible Region Visualization\",\"url\":\"https://miniwebtool.com/linear-programming-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"Satisfactory Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://kirkmcdonald.github.io/satisfactory-calculator/calc.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Satisfactory Tools calculators and their algorithms:\n\n## Satisfactory Calculator Tools\n\nThere are several production calculators available for the game Satisfactory:\n\nThe Satisfactory Tools is designed to calculate production lines, created by greeny with help from Lucek and other contributors.\n\nA collection of tools for the Satisfactory game includes a production planner that helps you find what you need to build the factory you want.\n\n## Algorithm Approaches\n\nRegarding the specific algorithms used:\n\nSome calculators use a mix of custom algorithms and ELK to provide coherent production lines to players.\n\nNotably, there is a Python script that uses scipy.optimize.linprog to calculate and optimize factory plans with respect to a highly configurable set of constraints. This is a linear programming approach using Python's optimization library.\n\nHowever, most of the search results focus on the general features and functionality of these calculators rather than detailed information about their underlying algorithms. The linear programming solver mentioned appears to be a separate tool using the simplex method, rather than the core algorithm of the main Satisfactory calculators.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"282373f1-5676-45b1-931f-c6d6862b2b54","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:16.549Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3621be7-ff13-425d-9fea-d90835e0f4f8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ae28d211-f361-4937-8ad9-cbc4d350d249","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a573a93d8823d4dbd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4eofzuFZdpdG7gdTYJ8MA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Factorio factory layout optimization MIP linear programming GitHub\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - reinderien/factorio: Factorio economic analysis · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/reinderien/factorio\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Rotsor/factorio-lp: factorio optimization: linear programming approach\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Rotsor/factorio-lp\"},{\"title\":\"FactorioLab\",\"url\":\"https://factoriolab.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Article Series About Smooth Factory Function and Factory Optimization Techniques - Factorio Forums\",\"url\":\"https://forums.factorio.com/viewtopic.php?t=110066\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - kevinburke/factorio-layout-optimizer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kevinburke/factorio-layout-optimizer\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Automatic Design of Factorio Blueprints Sean Patterson #\",\"url\":\"https://modref.github.io/papers/ModRef2023_TowardsAutomaticDesignOfFactorioBlueprints.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Factorio with Math (Linear Programming) - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gVXcc4CGEoo\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - elswindle/factorio_annealer: Program to generate a layout of factory cells in Factorio using simulated annealing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/elswindle/factorio_annealer\"},{\"title\":\"Alt-F4 #47 - Optimizing the Solution\",\"url\":\"https://alt-f4.blog/ALTF4-47/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - NeuralCoder3/factorio_recipe_planner: A planner to compute the optimal factory composition (machine and module wise) in the present of productivity and quality (Space Age)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NeuralCoder3/factorio_recipe_planner\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for Factorio factory layout optimization using MIP linear programming and GitHub projects:\n\n## Key GitHub Projects\n\nThe reinderien/factorio project uses constrained linear programming optimization to get analytical data about the game's economics and develop computed economies at scale. You can find this at https://github.com/reinderien/factorio.\n\nThe Rotsor/factorio-lp project is a factorio optimization tool using a linear programming approach. Available at https://github.com/Rotsor/factorio-lp.\n\nThe kevinburke/factorio-layout-optimizer uses existing blueprints and optimizes factory layout, though it doesn't chart space for connecting belts between blocks and blocks cannot rotate. You can view this at https://github.com/kevinburke/factorio-layout-optimizer.\n\nThe elswindle/factorio_annealer generates cost-optimized factory block layouts using simulated annealing optimization, available at https://github.com/elswindle/factorio_annealer.\n\n## MIP Solver Projects\n\nThe NeuralCoder3/factorio_recipe_planner computes optimal machine configurations using MIP/SMT solvers in the presence of quality and productivity modules. This project showcases support for z3, python-mip, and gurobi solvers.\n\n## Academic Work\n\nRecent research has focused on automatic design of Factorio blueprints using constraint programming to optimize blueprints while balancing correctness, optimality, and performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"aecb48a9-b262-4d9f-add6-0e38ec019501","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:16.645Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae28d211-f361-4937-8ad9-cbc4d350d249","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"974a85b7-279c-4d4f-9049-6a80f2e65055","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a573a93d8823d4dbd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012MgnC3xoJBMP5AhNAqxfZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Factorio blueprint optimizer SAT CP-SAT solver belt routing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - R-O-C-K-E-T/Factorio-SAT: Enhancing the Factorio experience with SAT solvers · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/R-O-C-K-E-T/Factorio-SAT\"},{\"title\":\"Using a SAT Solver to optimize balancers - Factorio Forums\",\"url\":\"https://forums.factorio.com/viewtopic.php?t=102232\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Solver Design: Automating Factorio Balancers\",\"url\":\"https://gianlucaventurini.com/posts/2024/factorio-sat\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - alegnani/verifactory: A verifier for Factorio blueprints, enabling one to automatically check logical properties\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/alegnani/verifactory\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - gianluca-venturini/factorio-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gianluca-venturini/factorio-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Solver Design: Automating Factorio Balancers | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=42524130\"},{\"title\":\"Factorio-SAT/README.md at main · R-O-C-K-E-T/Factorio-SAT\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/R-O-C-K-E-T/Factorio-SAT/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Friday Facts #176 - Belts optimization for 0.15 | Factorio\",\"url\":\"https://www.factorio.com/blog/post/fff-176\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Factorio with SAT solvers | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39344355\"},{\"title\":\"BeltRouter - Factorio Mods\",\"url\":\"https://mods.factorio.com/mod/BeltRouter/changelog\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about using SAT and CP-SAT solvers for Factorio blueprint optimization and belt routing:\n\n## SAT Solver Approaches\n\nThere's a project called Factorio-SAT that enhances the Factorio experience with SAT solvers. The approach represents tiles as a list of boolean (true/false) variables (input direction, output direction, underground state, splitter side, splitter id, colour), and clauses (rules/constraints) are written to restrict solutions to only valid balancers. This results in balancers that are within 1 tile of optimal and in practice no balancers have been found that exhibit this worst case.\n\n## CP-SAT Solver Implementation\n\nCP-SAT is a Satisfiability solver built at Google that can't deal with floating variables, so flows need to be discretized. Using CP-SAT for belt balancing from Factorio reveals that it's a NP complexity problem, though it looks innocuous at first.\n\n## Problem Challenges\n\nThe goal is to ensure all inputs are connected to all outputs while maintaining total maximum flow, with a Throughput-Unlimited Belt Balancer ensuring that every input flow is evenly distributed across all outputs.\n\n## Blueprint Verification\n\nBeyond optimization, using a SAT solver like z3, a blueprint graph is turned into a series of logical formulas and constraints that can be used to prove or disprove certain logical properties.\n\nThe search results show active research in applying constraint satisfaction and optimization solvers to automate Factorio factory design, particularly for the complex problem of designing efficient belt balancers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"84453744-3931-4aba-aa28-f7c774adcdc8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:16.871Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"974a85b7-279c-4d4f-9049-6a80f2e65055","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c3409710-a74a-4143-b41a-9b08deecdac6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a573a93d8823d4dbd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JJewdW6nh5xcemFZrw3mxS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Dyson Sphere Program calculator blueprint optimizer solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[DSPC] Dyson Sphere Program - Calculator | Gaming Tool/Wiki/Database to empower the players.\",\"url\":\"https://dyson-calculator.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Dyson Sphere Program Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://yesterdaysun.github.io/dsp-calculator/\"},{\"title\":\"The best Dyson Sphere Program calculator | PC Gamer\",\"url\":\"https://www.pcgamer.com/best-dyson-sphere-program-calculator-ratios/\"},{\"title\":\"Production planner / [DSPC] Dyson Sphere Program - Calculator | Gaming Tool/Wiki/Database to empower the players.\",\"url\":\"https://dyson-calculator.com/en/production-planner\"},{\"title\":\"Dyson Sphere Program - Calculator / AnthorNet - FullStack Web Developer\",\"url\":\"https://anthor.net/en/dyson-sphere-program\"},{\"title\":\"Dyson Sphere Program Calculator – Optimize Your Strategy – Made Calculators\",\"url\":\"https://madecalculators.com/dyson-sphere-program-calculator/\"},{\"title\":\"[SCIM] Satisfactory - Calculator | Gaming Tool/Wiki/Database to empower the players.\",\"url\":\"https://satisfactory-calculator.com/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - HuangFuSL/dsp-calculator: Desktop Dyson Sphere Program calculator · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/HuangFuSL/dsp-calculator\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - cabmoomoo/dsp-calc: Simple web-based calculator for the game Dyson Sphere Program. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cabmoomoo/dsp-calc\"},{\"title\":\"Dyson Sphere Program Calculator - Sage Calculator\",\"url\":\"https://sagecalculator.com/dyson-sphere-program-calculator/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are several tools and resources available for Dyson Sphere Program calculators, optimizers, and blueprint solvers:\n\n## Main Calculator Tools\n\n**Dyson-Calculator.com** - A comprehensive gaming tool/wiki/database with a production planner that helps calculate production needs and find what you need to build the factory you want.\n\n**FactorioLab Calculator for Dyson Sphere Program** - Described as the most complete calculator around, it uses the same interface as the original Factorio calculator but for calculating DSP's item recipes, featuring a clean, responsive, and highly customisable interface.\n\n**Dyson Sphere Program Calculator (yesterdaysun.github.io)** - Based on a Factorio calculator and created to apply lessons learned from developing that original calculator.\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n**Sage Calculator** - An easy, accurate calculator for optimized factory planning that calculates the number of assemblers needed, with an intuitive interface designed for both beginners and veteran players.\n\n**HuangFuSL/dsp-calculator (GitHub)** - A desktop Dyson Sphere Program calculator that can calculate the production chain of any item in the game and optimize proliferator usage.\n\n**GitHub cabmoomoo/dsp-calc** - A web-based calculator tool for calculating resource requirements and production ratios in Dyson Sphere Program.\n\nThese tools help players optimize factory layouts, plan production chains, calculate resource requirements, and design efficient blueprints for their Dyson Sphere projects.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"68955bd9-6e47-4414-8534-d189c19541da","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:17.682Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3409710-a74a-4143-b41a-9b08deecdac6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
